{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of quantum characteristic classes","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-quantum-characteristic-classes-exists"],"tags":["existence","characteristic-classes","cohomology"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumCharClasses.exists","text":"quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.md","leanSource":"quantum-characteristic-classes-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:quantum-characteristic-classes-exists\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Existence of quantum characteristic classes</em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\">quantum observable universe</a> with recursive brane tower <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{A_n\\}_{n \\ge 0}</code>. For every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\ge 0</code>, the <a href=\"#def:quantum-characteristic-classes\">quantum characteristic class</a></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\kappa_n \\in H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathcal{B})</code></pre>\n<p>exists as a well-defined cohomology class obstructing the lift <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{G}_n \\to \\mathfrak{G}_{n+1}</code>.</p>\n"}
